      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The debate often centers on the conflict between the principle of fair competition and the right to inclusion for transgender individuals. Some argue that competitive advantage is determined by biological sex, leading to the support of policies based on natal sex for fairness in many sports.\n\nConversely, proponents of gender identity argue that excluding trans individuals based on biological sex discriminates against them and that the focus should be on an individual's identity, not just their biology. This perspective emphasizes that well-regulated sports can accommodate diverse identities while still promoting competitive spirit for all.",
